config BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_SERIAL
	bool "cadr-serial"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_COMMON
	help
	  The CADR's serial line on a TCP socket, as muir's --serial
	  does.  The Signetics 2651 at IOBSER 0A12 is in the fabric and
	  keeps its own time; this program is the other end of the
	  RS-232 cable on J9.  A connection is the device plugging in,
	  which raises DSR, DCD and CTS, and hanging up drops them.

	  ONE DEVICE AT A TIME.  One thing is on the far end of a
	  null-modem cable, so a second connection is closed as it
	  arrives rather than shouting over the first.

	  NO RATE IS CHOSEN HERE.  The rate and the character frame are
	  whatever the machine has programmed into the 2651, and the far
	  end of a null-modem cable has no say in either.

	  It has an init script, as cadr-terminal does and unlike
	  cadr-console: somebody attaches when they want the line, and
	  nothing is on the bus while nobody is connected.
